{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellNeutrality","lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.HomologicalCondensation","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.fromUnion_lr_rigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.fromUnion_lr_rigidity","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L230-L245","doc":"**LR-rigidity proved for the trivial composite.** If both\nconstituents are self-conjugate, then the trivial union composite\nis itself self-conjugate. This is `DoubleMagicConjecture.lr_rigidity`\nproved without axioms in the trivial case — the disjoint multiset\nunion of two negation-symmetric multisets is negation-symmetric.\n\nThe honest LR fusion produces a *richer* composite via the\nLittlewood–Richardson rule, but content additivity and\nself-conjugacy preservation hold at the union level too, giving\na non-vacuous structural lower bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.fromUnion_kappa_zero_of_double_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.fromUnion_kappa_zero_of_double_magic","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L218-L228","doc":"**Concrete special case (fully proved, no axioms):** for the\ntrivial union composite, double-magic constituents force\n`κ_{ydA} = 0`. This is `doubleMagic_kappa_zero` specialised to\n`Composite.fromUnion`, where `ContentAdditive` is a real\ninstance rather than an axiomatic typeclass field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.composite_kappa_zero_of_double_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.composite_kappa_zero_of_double_magic","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L207-L216","doc":"Re-export: a double-magic composite has zero global Jucys–Murphy\ncharge.  Combines content additivity with the\nself-conjugate-zero-charge field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.composite_self_conjugate_of_double_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.composite_self_conjugate_of_double_magic","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L198-L205","doc":"Re-export: at a double-magic composite, the dominant module is\nself-conjugate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.lr_rigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.lr_rigidity","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L194-L194","doc":"LR-rigidity: the dominant composite of two self-conjugate\nsaturated constituents is itself self-conjugate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L191-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture","kind":"class","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L141-L196","doc":"**Conjecture 3 — Diagrammatic double-magic and LR-fusion rigidity.**\n\nFor saturated, self-conjugate constituents `λ_Z ⊢ Z` and `μ_N ⊢ N`\n(`Z, N ∈ 𝔐`), the LR-fusion at level `A = Z + N` is **rigid**: the dominant\ncomposite `ν_{ZN} ⊢ A` is itself self-conjugate. That is the `.md`'s claim\nand it is what `lr_rigidity` states.\n\n### 🛑 The second field is gone (2026-08-31), and it was FALSE\n\nUntil 2026-08-31 this class carried a second field:\n\n```lean\nmagic_iff_double_magic : ∀ (C : Composite),\n  (kappa C.ydA = 0 ∧ isSelfConjugate C.ydA ∧ C.ydA.n ∈ magicLadder)\n  ↔ IsDoubleMagic C\n```\n\nIt is removed for **two independent reasons**, both measured.\n\n**(1) The `A ∈ magicLadder` conjunct is not in the `.md`, and is false at\nevery physically intended instance.** The source block claims that the\ndominant `ν_{ZN}` is self-conjugate with `c(ν) = 0` and LR multiplicity one;\nit never claims the *composite strand count* `A = Z + N` is a magic number.\nMagic numbers are shell closures for a proton or neutron count separately,\nand the sum of two of them is essentially never one: of the seven observed\ndouble-magic nuclei — ⁴He (A=4), ¹⁶O (16), ⁴⁰Ca (40), ⁴⁸Ca (48), ⁵⁶Ni (56),\n¹³²Sn (132), ²⁰⁸Pb (208) — **not one** has `A ∈ {2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126}`.\nExhaustively, the only magic pair whose sum is magic at all is `8 + 20 = 28`.\n\n**(2) The `↔` was refutable, and the repair to `IsDoubleMagic` moves the\nfalsity rather than removing it.** With the old definition the `←`\ndirection failed at the empty composite (double-magic by triviality,\n`A = 0 ∉ magicLadder`). Adding the missing saturation makes `←` safe and\nbreaks `→` at the same point: `κ(∅) = 0` and `∅` is self-conjugate, but\n`0 ∉ magicLadder` so `∅` is not saturated. A converse of this shape cannot\nbe rescued by a non-degeneracy guard alone.\n\nThe converse was in any case a Lean addition: the removed docstring said\n*\"The reverse direction asserts that **only** double-magic compositions\nreach the magic ladder\"*, a claim the `.md` does not make.\n\n**Still not encoded**: the `.md` also claims the LR multiplicity is one\n(`c^{ν}_{λ,μ} = 1`, all others vanishing). That needs Littlewood–Richardson\ncoefficients, which this file does not carry, so it is stated in the\nnarrative and absent here. Recorded so the gap is visible rather than\nimplied.\n\nBean `qou-z9ws`; refutation of the old form in\n`docs/audits/2026-08-31-double-magic-conjecture-is-false.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.doubleMagic_kappa_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.doubleMagic_kappa_zero","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L130-L137","doc":"**Lemma (proved):** a double-magic composite has zero global\nJucys–Murphy charge `κ_{ydA} = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.kappa_zero_of_selfConj_constituents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.kappa_zero_of_selfConj_constituents","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L113-L128","doc":"**Lemma (proved):** self-conjugate constituents force zero global\nJucys–Murphy charge `κ_{ydA} = 0`. Direct from\n`kappa_zero_of_self_conjugate` (proved in ShellNeutrality) plus\ncontent additivity (typeclass field).\n\nStated on the two self-conjugacy facts rather than on `IsDoubleMagic`,\nbecause that is all the proof uses — saturation is irrelevant to it, and\nrequiring it would weaken the lemma for no gain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.IsDoubleMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.IsDoubleMagic","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L96-L111","doc":"The composite is **double magic** when both constituents are\nsaturated and self-conjugate (the LR-rigidity input).\n\n**Corrected 2026-08-31 — the `saturated` half was in this docstring but\nnot in the definition.** The `.md`\n([`conj:diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion`](../../../observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.md))\nopens *\"Let `Z, N ∈ 𝔐`\"* — both constituent levels are drawn from the magic\nset — and only then invokes `prop:categorical-neutrality-saturated-shells`\nfor self-conjugacy. The definition here carried the self-conjugacy alone, so\n\"double magic\" meant \"both constituents self-conjugate\", with no magic\nnumber involved anywhere. Under that reading the **empty** composite\n`⟨∅, ∅, ∅⟩` is double-magic — the empty diagram is trivially self-conjugate\n(`emptyDiagram_isSelfConjugate`) — which is what refuted the class below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.contentAdditive_fromUnion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.contentAdditive_fromUnion","kind":"instance","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L80-L92","doc":"The trivial union composite is content-additive *by direct\nproof* (no axiom). Provides a concrete instance of\n`ContentAdditive` against which downstream theorems can be\nsmoke-tested. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.fromUnion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.fromUnion","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L66-L78","doc":"The **trivial composite** built from the disjoint multiset union\nof constituents. This is *not* the LR-fusion composite — it is a\nstructural lower bound: any well-defined composite must agree\nwith this one on the level of content sums.\n\nExistence of this composite, together with the proved instance\n`contentAdditive_fromUnion`, shows that `ContentAdditive` is a\nconsistent typeclass (non-vacuous). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.ContentAdditive.kappa_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.ContentAdditive.kappa_add","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.ContentAdditive.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.ContentAdditive.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.ContentAdditive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.ContentAdditive","kind":"class","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L50-L64","doc":"**Content additivity** (provable from the LR rule, axiomatised\nhere at the abstract framework level): the Jucys–Murphy charge\nof the dominant composite equals the sum of the constituent\ncharges. This is the standard fact that contents add under\ntensor induction.\n\nA concrete *non-vacuous* instance is the disjoint-union\ncomposite `Composite.fromUnion`, where `ydA := ydZ ⊔ ydN`\nis the multiset disjoint union; in that case content additivity\nis *proved* directly from `kappa_unionDiagram`\n(see instance `contentAdditive_fromUnion`). The full LR-fusion\n`ydA` is conjecturally also content-additive but requires the\nLR rule to verify. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.mass_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.mass_eq","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Mass number condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.ydA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.ydA","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.ydN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.ydN","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.ydZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.ydZ","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite.mk","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.LRFusion.Composite","kind":"structure","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/LRFusion.lean#L38-L46","doc":"A composite nucleus: proton diagram `ydZ`, neutron diagram\n`ydN`, and the dominant LR-composite diagram `ydA` they fuse\nto. The composite has `n = Z + N` boxes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}